---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Services — Signal Advisory · Independent Technology Advisors"
  description="Four ways we lower your business technology costs. Provider negotiation, vendor consolidation, telecom expense management, and ongoing advisory — independent of every provider."
>
  <Nav />

  <section class="container mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 pb-20 pt-20 md:px-10 md:pt-28">
    <p class="mb-5 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-stone">What we do</p>
    <h1 class="display text-5xl font-light leading-[1.0] md:text-6xl">
      Four ways we lower<br />
      <em class="text-signal not-italic font-medium">your technology costs.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-10 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink/80">
      You pay us. The providers do not. That single fact changes what we are willing to tell
      you about which provider is best, when to renew, and where you are being overcharged.
      Engage us for one of these or all four.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- 01: Provider negotiation -->
  <section id="provider-negotiation" class="border-t border-ink/10 py-20">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 md:px-10">
      <div class="grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="md:col-span-1">
          <p class="mb-3 font-mono text-xs text-stone">01</p>
          <h2 class="display text-3xl font-medium">Provider negotiation</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-stone text-sm">
            Internet · Phone · Mobile · Cloud · Network
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="md:col-span-2 prose prose-lg max-w-none text-ink/80">
          <p>
            Every major business technology provider in the United States quoted on your
            behalf. AT&amp;T, Verizon, Lumen, Spectrum Business, Comcast Business, Cox, Frontier,
            and 200 more — across internet, phone systems, mobility, network, and cloud.
          </p>
          <p>
            How this differs from a typical agent: most agents are paid a residual commission
            by whichever provider you sign with. That means their advice on which provider
            to choose is downstream of which provider pays them more. We are paid by you
            directly. The recommendation we make is the same recommendation we would make
            for our own business.
          </p>
          <p><strong>Typical engagements include:</strong></p>
          <ul>
            <li>Renewals on existing contracts — start six to nine months before the renewal date to maintain real leverage</li>
            <li>New construction, mergers, and consolidating offices into one footprint</li>
            <li>Moving from older network technology (MPLS) to newer (SD-WAN, SASE)</li>
            <li>Replacing on-premises phone systems with cloud-based phone systems (UCaaS)</li>
            <li>Cleaning up corporate cell phone fleets across carriers</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 02: Vendor consolidation -->
  <section id="vendor-consolidation" class="border-t border-ink/10 bg-ink/[0.03] py-20">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 md:px-10">
      <div class="grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="md:col-span-1">
          <p class="mb-3 font-mono text-xs text-stone">02</p>
          <h2 class="display text-3xl font-medium">Vendor consolidation</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-stone text-sm">
            One bill · One contact · Less risk
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="md:col-span-2 prose prose-lg max-w-none text-ink/80">
          <p>
            Most mid-market companies have four to six different technology providers handling
            internet, phone, mobile, and cloud. That sprawl is expensive, slow, and hides where
            the money is actually going.
          </p>
          <p>
            We map every provider you currently use, every monthly cost, every renewal date,
            and every account contact. Then we identify what can responsibly be consolidated
            down — and just as important, what should stay separated to preserve redundancy
            and negotiating leverage.
          </p>
          <p>
            One useful number: simply producing the one-page vendor inventory is something
            most IT teams cannot do in an hour. Once it exists, the decisions about where to
            cut and where to keep things separate become straightforward.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 03: Telecom expense management -->
  <section id="tem" class="border-t border-ink/10 py-20">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 md:px-10">
      <div class="grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="md:col-span-1">
          <p class="mb-3 font-mono text-xs text-stone">03</p>
          <h2 class="display text-3xl font-medium">Telecom expense management</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-stone text-sm">
            Monthly bill auditing · Error recovery
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="md:col-span-2 prose prose-lg max-w-none text-ink/80">
          <p>
            Every month, we audit your telecom invoices against your contracts. We look for
            three things: billing errors the provider made, services you are paying for but
            no longer use, and unauthorized rate increases the provider sneaked in.
          </p>
          <p>
            The industry average is that 3 to 6 percent of telecom spend is recoverable
            through monthly auditing alone. On a company spending $20,000 a month on telecom,
            that is $7,000 to $14,000 a year back to your budget — without changing a single
            service.
          </p>
          <p><strong>What is included each month:</strong></p>
          <ul>
            <li>Line-by-line invoice review against your contract</li>
            <li>Disputes filed and tracked through to credit on the next invoice</li>
            <li>Identification of unused circuits, lines, and licenses to retire</li>
            <li>Inventory tracking — what services you have, where, and how much they cost</li>
            <li>Quarterly summary of recovered dollars and remaining opportunities</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Typically pays for itself within the first 60 days through credits we recover.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 04: Ongoing advisory -->
  <section id="ongoing-advisory" class="border-t border-ink/10 bg-ink/[0.03] py-20">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 md:px-10">
      <div class="grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="md:col-span-1">
          <p class="mb-3 font-mono text-xs text-stone">04</p>
          <h2 class="display text-3xl font-medium">Ongoing advisory</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-stone text-sm">
            Hourly or monthly retainer
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="md:col-span-2 prose prose-lg max-w-none text-ink/80">
          <p>
            Long-term independent guidance on the technology decisions your team makes every
            quarter. Hourly or monthly retainer. We do not take commissions tied to any
            specific recommendation, so the advice we give is the advice we would follow.
          </p>
          <p><strong>What we are typically asked to advise on:</strong></p>
          <ul>
            <li>Whether to renew an existing contract or move to a different provider</li>
            <li>How to structure a new contract (term length, escalator clauses, exit rights)</li>
            <li>Which architecture makes sense for the next five years (cloud, on-premises, hybrid)</li>
            <li>Implementation oversight when a vendor is delivering a project</li>
            <li>Second-opinion calls before signing anything material</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            If we cannot find at least $250 in monthly savings in an initial review, the
            review is free.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Pricing -->
  <section id="pricing" class="border-t border-ink/10 py-20">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 md:px-10">
      <p class="mb-4 text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-stone">Pricing</p>
      <h2 class="display mb-6 max-w-3xl text-4xl font-normal leading-tight md:text-5xl">
        Published rates. No retainers we can't justify.
      </h2>
      <p class="mb-16 max-w-3xl text-ink/70 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        We charge clients directly, not carriers. That means our recommendations on which provider, term, or architecture aren't downstream of who'd pay us a bigger commission. Three engagement structures depending on what you need.
      </p>

      <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="border border-ink/15 p-8">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs text-stone mb-3">HOURLY</p>
          <p class="display text-4xl font-medium text-ink mb-2">$250<span class="text-xl text-ink/60">/hr</span></p>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink/60 mb-6">Discrete questions, single-vendor review, second-opinion calls.</p>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-ink/75">
            <li>· Ad-hoc consultation</li>
            <li>· No minimum engagement</li>
            <li>· Billed monthly against time used</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="border-2 border-signal p-8 relative">
          <p class="absolute -top-3 left-8 bg-signal text-paper text-xs uppercase tracking-wider px-3 py-1">Most common</p>
          <p class="font-mono text-xs text-stone mb-3">CONTRACT REVIEW</p>
          <p class="display text-4xl font-medium text-ink mb-2">$2,500<span class="text-xl text-ink/60"> flat</span></p>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink/60 mb-6">One renewal, one decision, one defined deliverable.</p>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-ink/75">
            <li>· Invoice and contract audit</li>
            <li>· Marked-up MSA with renegotiation targets</li>
            <li>· Competitive baseline (3 carrier quotes)</li>
            <li>· 1-hour strategy session before you sign</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="border border-ink/15 p-8">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs text-stone mb-3">RETAINED</p>
          <p class="display text-4xl font-medium text-ink mb-2">From $3k<span class="text-xl text-ink/60">/mo</span></p>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink/60 mb-6">Ongoing vendor management, multi-site oversight, quarterly reviews.</p>
          <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-ink/75">
            <li>· Monthly invoice auditing</li>
            <li>· Renewal calendar management</li>
            <li>· Tier-2 ticket escalations</li>
            <li>· Quarterly business reviews</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-16 border-t border-ink/10 pt-12 bg-ink/[0.03] -mx-6 px-6 py-10 md:-mx-10 md:px-10">
        <div class="max-w-3xl">
          <p class="font-mono text-xs text-signal mb-3">THE GUARANTEE</p>
          <h3 class="display text-2xl font-medium text-ink mb-4">
            If we can't find at least $250/month in savings, the review is free.
          </h3>
          <p class="text-ink/75 leading-relaxed">
            We start every engagement with a free 30-minute scoping call and an invoice review. If
            we don't see a clear path to at least $250 in monthly recurring savings on your
            existing IT spend, you don't pay for the time we spent. No invoice, no follow-up. We
            offer this because in 9 out of 10 mid-market reviews we run, the savings clear the
            threshold inside the first 20 minutes.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="border-t border-ink/10 bg-ink py-24 text-paper">
    <div class="container mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 text-center md:px-10">
      <h2 class="display mb-6 text-4xl font-normal leading-tight md:text-5xl">
        Ready to look at the numbers?
      </h2>
      <p class="mb-10 text-lg text-paper/60 leading-relaxed">
        Send us your last carrier invoice. We'll mark up what we'd renegotiate, no obligation.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
        <a
          href="/audit"
          class="inline-block rounded-sm bg-signal px-8 py-4 text-sm font-semibold text-paper hover:bg-paper hover:text-ink transition-colors"
        >
          Free invoice audit
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://calendly.com/signaladvise-info/30min"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block rounded-sm border border-paper/30 px-8 py-4 text-sm font-medium hover:border-paper transition-colors"
        >
          Schedule a 30-min call
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Base>
